  <name>Pochette</name>
  <summary>Listen to Qobuz, album by album</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.mcrampon">
    <name>Matthieu Crampon</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Pochette is a native player for Qobuz, built around albums: your library of whole albums,
      played from the first track to the last.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Albums: your saved albums, to search, filter by genre and decade, sort, or play at random</li>
      <li>Discover: Qobuz's new releases, press awards and ideal discography, by genre</li>
      <li>Lyrics that follow the song, looked up on LRCLIB while you show them</li>
      <li>Hi-Res streaming, up to what your subscription allows</li>
      <li>Media keys and desktop media controls, through MPRIS</li>
      <li>Your desktop's accent color, light and dark modes</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Pochette requires a paid Qobuz subscription. It is not certified by Qobuz and not
      affiliated with Qobuz.
    </p>
  </description>

  <screenshots>
    <screenshot type="default">
      <caption>Discover, in light mode</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mcrampon/pochette/master/data/screenshots/discover-light.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>Playing an album, in dark mode</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mcrampon/pochette/master/data/screenshots/playing-dark.png</image>
    </screenshot>
  </screenshots>

